<title>USA: U.S. DAP Gulf prices up on Mississippi problems.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP Gulf prices up on Mississippi problems.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices for diammonium phosphate (DAP) at the U.S. Gulf were slightly higher in the wake of high water on the Mississippi, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The entire river system is shut down, so if you have a barge in the right place, your prices are higher,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>			     Dlrs/short ton	 Chg from Monday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla		175-176		  unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf	  188-190		  up 2-up 1</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf		170-174		  unc</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
